WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.929
Movies and Weekend Plans.

2
00:00:02.209 --> 00:00:06.710
Day 57 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.484
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.764 --> 00:00:16.719
Today's goal: make plans with friends, book tickets, talk about films and shows, and give opinions and recommendations.

5
00:00:18.069 --> 00:00:18.922
Part 1.

6
00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:20.205
Making plans.

7
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:22.799
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:24.551
Suggest, and Respond.

9
00:00:24.831 --> 00:00:26.943
Do you want to watch a movie this weekend?:

10
00:00:27.223 --> 00:00:27.884
Sure!

11
00:00:28.164 --> 00:00:28.975
Which one?

12
00:00:29.255 --> 00:00:30.791
How about Saturday evening?:

13
00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:34.249
Saturday works for me. / Sunday is better for me.

14
00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:36.513
Shall we go for the 7 pm show?:

15
00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:37.604
Perfect.

16
00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:40.060
Let's meet at the mall at 6:30.:

17
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.257
See you there!

18
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:43.244
Are you up for a trek on Sunday?:

19
00:00:43.524 --> 00:00:45.401
I'd love to, but I'm a bit tired.

20
00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:46.855
Maybe next week?

21
00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:49.079
Part 2.

22
00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:50.405
Booking tickets.

23
00:00:51.655 --> 00:00:54.279
Two tickets for the 7:15 show, please.

24
00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:56.308
Recliner seats if available.

25
00:00:56.588 --> 00:00:58.423
Are there any seats in the middle row?

26
00:00:58.703 --> 00:01:00.431
Is there a discount on weekdays?

27
00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:02.865
Can I cancel the booking if plans change?

28
00:01:04.215 --> 00:01:05.111
Part 3.

29
00:01:05.391 --> 00:01:07.077
Talking about films and shows.

30
00:01:08.327 --> 00:01:09.671
Here is a quick table:

31
00:01:09.951 --> 00:01:11.145
Ask, and Answer.

32
00:01:11.425 --> 00:01:13.025
What kind of movies do you like?:

33
00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:15.055
I like thrillers and comedies.

34
00:01:15.335 --> 00:01:16.231
Not horror!

35
00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:17.556
What's it about?:

36
00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:20.865
It's about a cricketer who makes a comeback after an injury.

37
00:01:21.145 --> 00:01:22.084
Who's in it?:

38
00:01:22.364 --> 00:01:24.433
It stars... and it's directed by...

39
00:01:24.713 --> 00:01:25.631
How was it?:

40
00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:29.089
It was brilliant or okay or a bit slow or too long.

41
00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.649
Would you recommend it?:

42
00:01:30.929 --> 00:01:36.071
Definitely, especially the second half. / Not really, wait for it on OTT.

43
00:01:36.351 --> 00:01:37.503
Have you watched...?:

44
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:40.215
Yes, I loved it! / No, is it good?

45
00:01:41.565 --> 00:01:48.626
Opinion words: gripping, hilarious, touching, predictable, slow, overrated, a must-watch, no spoilers, please!

46
00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:50.893
Part 4.

47
00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:53.776
Conversation 1: making weekend plans.

48
00:01:55.026 --> 00:01:57.053
Here is how the conversation goes.

49
00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:58.997
Any plans for the weekend?

50
00:01:59.277 --> 00:02:00.258
Not yet.

51
00:02:00.538 --> 00:02:03.205
Do you want to watch the new Malayalam thriller?

52
00:02:03.485 --> 00:02:05.298
Everyone's talking about it.

53
00:02:05.578 --> 00:02:06.239
Sure!

54
00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:08.759
Is it in theatres or on OTT?

55
00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.191
In theatres.

56
00:02:10.471 --> 00:02:13.159
How about the 7 pm show on Saturday?

57
00:02:13.439 --> 00:02:14.719
Saturday works.

58
00:02:14.999 --> 00:02:16.514
Should we have dinner after?

59
00:02:17.864 --> 00:02:19.464
The conversation continues.

60
00:02:19.744 --> 00:02:20.704
Good idea.

61
00:02:20.984 --> 00:02:23.757
There's a nice Chettinad place near the mall.

62
00:02:24.037 --> 00:02:25.083
Perfect.

63
00:02:25.363 --> 00:02:26.899
Will you book the tickets?

64
00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:30.421
Yes, I'll book two recliners and send you the details.

65
00:02:31.771 --> 00:02:32.731
Part 5.

66
00:02:33.011 --> 00:02:35.187
Conversation 2: after the movie.

67
00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:38.464
Here is how the conversation goes.

68
00:02:38.744 --> 00:02:40.109
So, what did you think?

69
00:02:40.389 --> 00:02:41.456
I loved it!

70
00:02:41.736 --> 00:02:46.237
The first half was a bit slow, but the twist at the interval was brilliant.

71
00:02:46.517 --> 00:02:47.669
I know!

72
00:02:47.949 --> 00:02:49.656
I didn't see it coming at all.

73
00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.155
And the background music was amazing.

74
00:02:52.435 --> 00:02:53.907
Who was the composer?

75
00:02:54.187 --> 00:02:55.787
Sushin Shyam, I think.

76
00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.667
What did you think of the ending?

77
00:02:59.017 --> 00:03:00.617
The conversation continues.

78
00:03:00.897 --> 00:03:02.945
Honestly, a little predictable.

79
00:03:03.225 --> 00:03:05.273
But overall, it's a must-watch.

80
00:03:05.553 --> 00:03:06.427
Agreed.

81
00:03:06.707 --> 00:03:10.206
Should we watch the director's earlier film on Netflix next weekend?

82
00:03:10.486 --> 00:03:11.873
Sure, let's do that!

83
00:03:13.223 --> 00:03:14.161
Part 6.

84
00:03:14.441 --> 00:03:15.487
Speak today.

85
00:03:16.737 --> 00:03:21.707
Tell someone about the last movie or series you watched: what it's about, and your opinion.

86
00:03:21.987 --> 00:03:25.763
Make one weekend plan in English using How about...? or Shall we...?

87
00:03:27.113 --> 00:03:28.649
That's the end of this lesson.

88
00:03:28.929 --> 00:03:33.580
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

89
00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:39.983
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

